{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DPL", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-relative-morphisms}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c1e94c26523d12a6feb0f3dbd4af7732749cb20a7e0b9357bd53d91a6456ca6b", "source_text": "Properties of relative morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a7ee5194bb063cd9fca8eec819c959d74016b5681d1e832b9e6f441e48aac798", "unit_id": "tag:0DPL:title"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DPL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$Y \\to B$", "MATH_0006": "$X \\to B$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathit{Mor}_B(Y, X)$", "MATH_0008": "$B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-proposition-Mor}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c37e89ef738041df082ab86b6a7f98efdb2aa5f51dc99a0b2ec469b68fa2d6b0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b99e4ca73b62ef77ac5b3267b4a4af46fedfa596a704b39e4b51435bf52ddc6c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be an algebraic space. Let <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> be algebraic spaces\nover <MATH_0004> such that <MATH_0005> is flat, proper, and of finite presentation\nand <MATH_0006> is separated and of finite presentation.\nThen the functor <MATH_0007> of relative morphisms\nis an algebraic space locally of finite presentation over <MATH_0008>.\nSee Quot, Proposition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8048a693e15cbbf1423493df92b1dd37308114996f2b2dd7cd61233baa20d7fc", "unit_id": "tag:0DPL:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DPL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathit{Mor}_B(Y, X) \\to B$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-Mor-diagonal-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0589f392639f334fe8714038ec3f2ab12f79e41e51d0a49fdefd4f7f146d0dfe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5c0b2a2acd965ded25746b0c7ea2da062218baf22d82143db0f71a845b149e37", "source_text": "The diagonal of <MATH_0001> is a closed immersion\nof finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cb9347bd50ad17c047b862bda3adb414147b504e076241fb64d264874aaf010e", "unit_id": "tag:0DPM:statement"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DPL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathit{Mor}_B(Y, X) \\to \\Hilbfunctor_{Y \\times_B X/B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-lemma-Mor-into-Hilb-open}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-hilb-diagonal-closed}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cc20698481ea89911a4d97e91a7dc4897365ceb0dfc3711f5982d4cf4987d22c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:93e750683127351b374b26443baaafa7a0e3e6bf03e235a5bd2dfbb74b07c58b", "source_text": "There is an open immersion\n<MATH_0001>, see\nQuot, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThus the lemma follows from\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7fec32ffb2519a5d3dfcc96b8d9d955ed5e3615b515ccab6a5d1c23aa1cdb3f7", "unit_id": "tag:0DPM:proof"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DPL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathit{Mor}_B(Y, X) \\to B$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-Mor-s-lfp}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0589f392639f334fe8714038ec3f2ab12f79e41e51d0a49fdefd4f7f146d0dfe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b50b0ed53ec6b54e1dc80342aa749034f6bb0bcfd0045894d3b1fe8f3abf672", "source_text": "The morphism <MATH_0001> is separated\nand locally of finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8d63642ca3da00213568eea75fe4787c5007556a0627e4f4c401159abd1658a6", "unit_id": "tag:0DPN:statement"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DPL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathit{Mor}_B(Y, X) \\to B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-Mor-diagonal-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{quot-proposition-Mor}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0589f392639f334fe8714038ec3f2ab12f79e41e51d0a49fdefd4f7f146d0dfe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2e4be7e220a5b07ea29d2712795da6d4511a38097a14c31db2d011a85696ec2", "source_text": "To check <MATH_0001> is separated we have to\nshow that its diagonal is a closed immersion. This\nis true by Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThe second statement is part of\nQuot, Proposition <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f3e0b976f1d58ea30fff8c252425d2be46c76681454ad6daf38b1d6d36614b6b", "unit_id": "tag:0DPN:proof"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DPL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B, X, Y$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to B$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathit{Isom}_B(Y, X) \\subset \\mathit{Mor}_B(Y, X)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-Isom-in-Mor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2f667d9222fb28d43ade0b0c3bf075707e672b31743cb05759a1baea2b0f6138", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b019aea7750976ad529beea5354f89cbea3ee6790a78396b2ce2af5523bb8bff", "source_text": "With <MATH_0001> as in the introduction of this section, in addition\nassume <MATH_0002> is proper. Then the\nsubfunctor <MATH_0003>\nof isomorphisms is an open subspace.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:821424f3f2e0f0ca25646a3632309e95d41548da8f48c21ac1b66e1196708263", "unit_id": "tag:0DPP:statement"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DPL", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-more-morphisms-lemma-where-isomorphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a3892d09cf6a4ea60bf6f4edeaa9559cf3636f92287adf7a2bcf9397cf49f785", "source_text": "Follows immediately from More on Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5a16e682ea9385e1fa2ef9354c51bdfab40b72237a5a0060130e09bc77cfb51d", "unit_id": "tag:0DPP:proof"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0DPL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B, X, Y$", "MATH_0002": "$I$", "MATH_0003": "$i \\in I$", "MATH_0004": "$E_i \\in D(\\mathcal{O}_{Y \\times_B X})$", "MATH_0005": "$P : I \\to \\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\mathit{Mor}_B(Y, X) \\subset\n\\Hilbfunctor_{Y \\times_B X/B}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\mathit{Mor}^P_B(Y, X) =\n\\mathit{Mor}_B(Y, X) \\cap \\Hilbfunctor^P_{Y \\times_B X/B}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Hilbfunctor^P_{Y \\times_B X/B}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\mathit{Mor}^P_B(Y, X) \\longrightarrow \\mathit{Mor}_B(Y, X)\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$I$", "MATH_0011": "$B$", "MATH_0012": "$I = \\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0013": "$E_i = \\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes i}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{O}_{Y \\times_B X}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathit{Mor}^{P, \\mathcal{L}}_B(Y, X)$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{remark-Mor-numerical}\n", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-lemma-Mor-into-Hilb-open}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-hilb-numerical}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}[", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ace580cc8efc3acb1ca935d0d94d2b16e0e53279f6c4bd47d4777406c7f47d55", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7cd8f9fe9b92d71090e7ca4394f71e5063dd47bb7f5d868b1a9b108e05f43974", "source_text": "Numerical invariants<OWNARGEND_0001>Let <MATH_0001> be as in the introduction to this section.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a set and for <MATH_0003> let\n<MATH_0004> be perfect.\nLet <MATH_0005> be a function. Recall that\n<MATH_0006>\nis an open subspace, see Quot, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThus we can define\n<MATH_0007>\nwhere <MATH_0008> is as in\nRemark <REF_0002>. The morphism\n<MATH_0009>\nis a flat closed immersion which is an open and closed immersion\nfor example if <MATH_0010> is finite, or <MATH_0011> is locally Noetherian, or\n<MATH_0012>, <MATH_0013>\nfor some invertible <MATH_0014>-module <MATH_0015>.\nIn the last case we sometimes use the notation\n<MATH_0016>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:77dd46fa723673b51a7a1149877f246e0642d4e50bedc52faa48e4af35b31ae0", "unit_id": "tag:0DPQ:statement"}
